  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 85%, transparent);
  backdrop-filter: saturate(1.2) blur(8px); position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 20; }
.topbar h1, .topbar h2 { margin: 0; font-size: var(--fs-md); font-weight: 600; flex: 1; min-width: 0;
  overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.topbar .actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px; }
.topbar .divider { width: 1px; height: 20px; background: var(--line); margin: 0 6px; }
```

---

## 6. Home page ("New project")

The pattern used by the big chat products: one strong question, the composer centred and above the fold, and a few helpful starting points. For CATE, also show **team status**, because NN/g says empty states should show system status and direct routes into key tasks.

```
                 Good evening. What should your AI team work on?
     Your supervisor plans it, splits it, and hands each part to the best model.
   ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ Describe your project…                                                │
   │                                                                       │
   │ 📎  ✦ Models: auto   ⫼ Compare                               ◔  ➤    │
   └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
     ● Claude ×2 ready   ● ChatGPT ready   ◐ Groq 18% left   ○ Gemini not connected →
   ┌ Research a topic ┐ ┌ Write a document ┐ ┌ Change CATE's code ┐ ┌ Compare models ┐
   │ with sources…    │ │ draft + review…  │ │ opens a PR…        │ │ same prompt…   │
   └──────────────────┘ └──────────────────┘ └────────────────────┘ └────────────────┘
     Recent projects                                                    View all →
     • Refine CATE design              working · 3 tasks            2 min ago
     • Competitor analysis             waiting for review           1 h ago
```
- The **status strip** reuses data the composer already has (`data.usage.rows`). Each chip links to `/models#<id>`. If *nothing* is connected, or the supervisor is off, replace the strip with one clear card: "Connect your first model (2 minutes) →" linking to the models page's add section. Today a missing supervisor only shows as a banner on the models page.
- **Suggestion cards** gain a 16px icon and a two-line description, and fill the composer when clicked (`.suggestion` already exists).
- **Recent projects** helps people coming back. The sidebar has them too, but on mobile the sidebar is hidden.

