---

## 7. Models & connections page: easy to read, and clear how to add more

Today (`app/(app)/models/page.js` + `components/ModelsPanel.js`), each connection card shows everything at once: limits, budget, every model checkbox, 7 role dropdowns and connect steps. "Add a connection" sits at the bottom, below several cards. The fix: **"add" goes first and gets its own guide; cards get short; configuration is hidden until asked for.**

### Page structure
```
Models & connections                                        [ + Add model or API ]
Your AI accounts and free APIs, and which model does which job.

┌ How to add a model ───────────────────────────────────────────────── (hide) ┐
│ ① Pick a type          ② Get a key or token        ③ Save it in GitHub      ④ Press Resume │
│ Claude / ChatGPT plan   one command or one link     Secrets → name shown     it runs on the next job │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

