## 8. "Node designs": a team map for the connections page

The user asked about "better node designs". A node diagram fits CATE well because it *is* a graph: **You → Supervisor → Connections (accounts/APIs) → Models**, with edges showing which models each account may use and edge labels for the job kinds routed there.

Two ways to build it:
- **Simple (no dependency):** three CSS-grid columns (Supervisor | Connections | Models) with an SVG overlay for curved edges. Good enough for under ~15 nodes and fully static.
- **Interactive:** [`@xyflow/react`](https://reactflow.dev/examples) (MIT). The free examples cover custom nodes, node toolbar (Pause/Configure on the selected node), edge labels and dagre/elk layout. Auto-layout helpers in the Pro tier are **not** needed for a 3-column graph; set positions by column. Adds about one dependency to `web/package.json`.

